hon3 /work/experiments/current_path_calculation.py > /work/experiments/current_path_calculation.log\ncat /work/experiments/current_path_calculation.log\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\npairs={'PCB J1 holes':('/candidate/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb',21684,21727),'PCB ground zone':('/candidate/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb',69477,69494),'termination population':('/candidate/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch',2662,2702),'PCB R36 DNP':('/candidate/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb',14730,14755)}\nlines=[]\nfor label,(path,a,z) in pairs.items():\n lines.append(label+' — inputs/'+path.removeprefix('/candidate/')+'\\\\n')\n raw=Path(path).read_text().splitlines();lines.extend(f'{i+1}: {raw[i]}\\\\n' for i in range(a-1,z))\nPath('/work/experiments/native_excerpts.txt').write_text(''.join(lines))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"/HeaterNeg\": {\n    \"series_chain_length_mm\": 109.9709,\n    \"chain_widths_mm\": [\n      0.6\n    ],\n    \"estimated_trace_resistance_ohm_20C\": 0.09028087219047622,\n    \"voltage_drop_V_per_A\": 0.09028087219047622,\n    \"copper_power_W_per_A_squared\": 0.09028087219047622\n  },\n  \"/HeaterNeg2\": {\n    \"series_chain_length_mm\": 156.481,\n    \"chain_widths_mm\": [\n      0.6\n    ],\n    \"estimated_trace_resistance_ohm_20C\": 0.12846344952380956,\n    \"voltage_drop_V_per_A\": 0.12846344952380956,\n    \"copper_power_W_per_A_squared\": 0.12846344952380956\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /work/experiments/REVIEW_NOTES.md <<'EOF'\n# Physical initial review — experiment record\n\nCandidate d5b8384d1b2948621e1c1b2dc675affa4fc13959286eea50af3e9df6c5dcd0d8\nRun 8bf132e9-a698-44e0-878f-52cc0c3c103b\nPacket 7d6ad171f58d1613d318a67536493e0664238a9b72425bbe0a688036e0181b2d\n\n## Source and boundaries\n\nRead candidate native PCB, project rules, relevant schematic/symbol/footprint definitions, and complete supplied DRC/ERC/netlist/geometry JSON records under /evidence. No prior-review experiment or judgment was used. No credential files read. No candidate file written or copper refilled. A footprint was moved/rotated only in an unsaved in-memory object to compare normalized J2 pad locations, not to propose or test a fix.\n\nCommands and generated files below are under /work/experiments, cited as review-work/physical/experiments/. Inputs remain cited as inputs/project/.... Supplied evidence remains cited as work/<check>/....\n\n## Tools and commands\n\nKiCad CLI and pcbnew 10.0.7; Python 3.12.3. pcbnew imports print three PROPERTY_ENUM assertions but successfully load the board and return measurements; these messages are not treated as electrical results. Initial inventory used pwd, ls, rg --files, selected rg -n native UUID/rule searches, and reads of fp-lib-table/sym-lib-table and the PCB stackup. No applicable AGENTS.md was found in the working source inventory.\n\n- \"'`run_checks.py`, `commands.json`, and command_*.stdout/stderr record commands, versions, outcomes, independent native DRC, separated PTH/NPTH drill export and saved-copper SVG export. No refill/save switches used.\n- The first independent DRC had 156 entries because this review environment initially lacked stock global footprint table entries (129 library issues). The 13 physical error entries, 14 silk entries, 114 parity entries and zero unconnected items agreed with supplied evidence. This environment/configuration difference is not a candidate electrical defect.\n- `recheck_with_stock.py` writes explicit global library tables only in experiments/kicad-config and reruns native checks. `stock_commands.json` and stock_command_*.stdout/stderr record the exact commands/environment. Final `stock_drc.json` reproduces the supplied counts exactly: 142 violations, 114 parity entries, zero unconnected items. All 13 error entries are excluded:true: 3 starved thermals, 5 padstack, 5 annular-width. Neither exclusions nor CLI status 0 prove qualification or correct electrical behavior.\n- Independent native XML export `independent_design.xml` has 10 sheet instances, 139 components and 199 nets; named net membership exactly matches supplied XML. `verification_results.json` records comparison and hashes. The uppercase disposable VR Conditioner sheet alias and original lowercase file have identical SHA256 377a2691ec878301977100851c40e302b2b7864d88cc27c6c305c03bbf14e15b. This does not close the filename issue in the separate original checkout.\n- `/usr/bin/python3 inspect_board.py > board_inspection.log 2>&1` reads native geometry, reports hole annuli, DNP population, selected pads and zones, and compares J2 against the bundled symbol-selected footprint. First attempt failed JSON serialization of a KiCad UTF8 type; preserved in board_inspection_first_attempt.log. Corrected serialization succeeds. UUID fields use AsString, not SWIG object addresses. Board hash remains 4e059d571e0f46911d9101b86c8178298cefb866e2f19d5295a30c35dadedd53.\n- `check_audit.json` was produced by Python JSON reads of complete supplied reports, netlist and geometry. Pin parity method: build maps ref.pad -> named net from every numbered PCB pad and every schematic net node, compare each key and value. All 659 unique ref.pad keys match; no extras/missing pins. This checks assignments, not analog function or connection resistance. Route inventory groups native segments/vias by net and sums segment lengths; inventories are not path impedance or current ratings.\n- J2 has 107 saved pads versus 96 in the symbol-selected bundled polygonus footprint. Every one of the 96 common numbered pad positions has the same translation after orientation normalization. The extra USB/SWD pins and origin differ. This is insufficient to claim mechanical incompatibility; no such finding is made.\n- `kicad-cli pcb export drill --excellon-separate-th --generate-report ...` creates drill files without changing the board. PTH header explicitly specifies Plated. T10C2.200 hits X75.55Y-39.34 and X199.65Y-39.34; T12C4.000 hits X71.95Y-35.49, X120.0Y-28.49, X203.25Y-35.49. NPTH file has no hits. Thus five questionable holes really export as PTH, not NPTH.\n- `rsvg-convert -w 1800 -o front_saved.png front_saved.svg` renders exported F.Cu plus Edge.Cuts. Visually inspected the saved front copper/outline. No full multi-layer field analysis or assembly collision check was performed.\n- `molex_fetch.json` records attempted primary connector drawing retrieval: curl --location --fail --max-time 25 https://www.molex.com/pdm_docs/sd/643330100_sd.pdf. It failed with curl 6, DNS resolution failure. No manufacturer plating, fit or tolerance requirement is inferred from this unavailable source.\n\n## Measurements, calculations and interpretation\n\nFive unnumbered J1 pads specify thru_hole, *.Cu and pad diameter equal drill diameter (three 4.0 mm, two 2.2 mm). Annular ring calculation (pad diameter - drill diameter)/2 = 0 mm; saved project rule min_via_annular_width is 0.1 mm. Each has two excluded native errors with empty exclusion comment. Their lack of a net prevents interpreting them as a demonstrated signal open. The physical finding concerns native manufacturing geometry and the actual plated drill classification; no fab rejection or mechanical failure is asserted.\n\nC15.2, U7.4, C14.2 are GND pads in zone bc540b8b-3ffa-4b00-b211-3a91191a1f6d. Both supplied and independent DRC identify one F.Cu spoke, versus min_resolved_spokes=2. Native ground zone has 0.3 mm thermal gap and 0.4 mm bridge setting. All three are explicitly excluded without comments. This is a saved-rule exception, not proof of an open circuit, inadequate ampacity or an overheating component. Zero unconnected items does not verify spoke redundancy.\n\nR36 and R37 are each 120 ohms, DNP and excluded from schematic BOM; saved PCB also marks them DNP. Each spans CAN2+ and CAN2-. Both WBO transceivers, J2.73/.74 and J1.15/.11 share the bus. Default carrier resistor conductance is 0 S; one fitted resistor would give 120 ohms and two would give 60 ohms in parallel. These are resistor-population calculations, not measured total bus impedance: brain-module and external harness termination are outside supplied native carrier implementation. An isolated carrier could lack resistive termination; a correctly terminated external/module bus could be entirely intentional. This uncertainty is a concern only, with no categorical claim that the short internal bus fails.\n\n`python3 current_path_calculation.py > current_path_calculation.log` records a conditional resistance calculation from saved B.Cu heater-negative chains. Excluding the module pad11-pad12 stub under the explicit equipotential assumption, paths are 109.9709 mm and 156.481 mm, 0.6 mm wide. With saved 35 um copper and assumed copper resistivity 1.724e-8 ohm*m at 20 C, R=rho*L/(w*t) gives 0.09028 and 0.12846 ohms. V=IR and P=I''^2 R are provided as coefficients only. No load current, thermal boundary, contact/barrel resistance, copper tolerance or operating temperature has been established. No ampacity, temperature rise or thermal defect is inferred from these widths or resistances.\n\n## Explicit coverage omissions\n\nNo refill verification; only saved zone state. No physical prototype, resistance/temperature measurements, CAN signaling stimulus, bit-rate/edge/cable model, impedance/TDR or full return-path field solver. No full module internals (including brain CAN termination or integrated FOME-MC), complete current budget, fuse coordination, load duty cycles or thermal qualification. No automotive transient, ignition energy, wideband stability or EMC qualification. No exhaustive mechanical 3D clearances, connector drawing tolerances, fab process capability, solder/reflow qualification or manufacturing approval. Native missing-courtyard, PTH/NPTH-inside-courtyard and several other checks are disabled; copper-edge minimum is 0.0 mm, so this is not validation of a fabricator'\"'s edge allowance. Not every ERC/library/parity warning was individually adjudicated against actual component datasheets; only report coverage and selected native physical issues were investigated. No new requirements, ratings or SPICE device models were assigned.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib,hashlib,json\nb=pathlib.Path('/work/experiments');p=pathlib.Path('/candidate/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb')\nassert hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()=='4e059d571e0f46911d9101b86c8178298cefb866e2f19d5295a30c35dadedd53'\n(b/'artifact_manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({str(p.relative_to(b)):{'bytes':p.stat().st_size,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()} for p in sorted(b.rglob('*')) if p.is_file() and p.name\"'!='\"'artifact_manifest.json'},indent=2))\nprint('Candidate PCB hash unchanged; experiment notes and manifest saved.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
